Title: AROS: drop '.' path components before system calls
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: LibreSprite creates drawers by asking for "dir/." (palettes, sessions). On the Raspberry Pi ENVARC: is on FAT, whose handler rejects the "." name: the first start stopped with "Error creating directory ENVARC:LibreSprite/palettes/.: Invalid argument". SFS on x86 accepted it.
Change: base::to_system_path (patch 0025) removes "/./" and trailing "/." components before every file-system call on AROS.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only
Verification: Raspberry Pi (pool rpi-1, non-smp, nightly 20261110, 2026-11-16): first start with no ENVARC:LibreSprite works; new sprite, drawing, PNG save with Enter, Intuition menu, clean exit; AUTO chose OpenGL ("GUI_RENDERER=AUTO, gl.library present: OpenGL") and the system stayed up.
Removal: AROS-specific.
---
diff --git a/src/base/system_path_aros.cpp b/src/base/system_path_aros.cpp
index 47f8e6db921c5dec6a022acc23ed448ebb904dcb..36cdb178d52000ce5a7b6c0b71c80d5303d2d290 100644
--- a/src/base/system_path_aros.cpp
+++ b/src/base/system_path_aros.cpp
@@ -74,8 +74,23 @@ namespace {
 
 } // anonymous namespace
 
-std::string to_system_path(const std::string& utf8)
+// "." components ("dir/." to make sure a drawer exists, "a/./b"): POSIX
+// names for the same directory, but not names AmigaDOS knows; FAT on the
+// Raspberry Pi rejects them ("Invalid argument").
+static std::string without_dot_components(const std::string& path)
 {
+  std::string out = path;
+  std::string::size_type pos;
+  while ((pos = out.find("/./")) != std::string::npos)
+    out.erase(pos, 2);
+  while (out.size() >= 2 && out.compare(out.size() - 2, 2, "/.") == 0)
+    out.erase(out.size() - 2);
+  return out;
+}
+
+std::string to_system_path(const std::string& path)
+{
+  const std::string utf8 = without_dot_components(path);
   if (is_ascii(utf8))
     return utf8;
   std::string out;
